      "hints": [
        "Set $a + 11d = 17$ and $\\frac{31}{2}(2a + 30d) = 31(a + 15d) = 1023$.",
        "Solve simultaneously to find $d = 4, a = -27$.",
        "Evaluate 31st term: $T_{31} = a + 30d = 93$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set up equations for the 12th term and the sum of the first 31 terms:\n$$T_{12} = a + 11d = 17$$\n$$S_{31} = \\frac{31}{2}(2a + 30d) = 31(a + 15d) = 1023 \\implies a + 15d = \\frac{1023}{31} = 33$$",
        "Subtract the first equation from the second to find the common difference $d$:\n$$(a + 15d) - (a + 11d) = 33 - 17 \\implies 4d = 16 \\implies d = 4$$",
        "Find the first term $a$:\n$$a = 17 - 11(4) = 17 - 44 = -27$$",
        "Calculate the 31st term $T_{31}$:\n$$T_{31} = a + 30d = -27 + 30(4) = -27 + 120 = 93$$"
      ],
